# Accessibility

Every interactive surface must work with keyboard, screen reader, touch (≥44px), and reduced motion — across phone, tablet, desktop, landscape, and high-DPI.

## Requirements

| Area | Rule |
|---|---|
| Keyboard | Native `<button>` / `<a>` / labeled inputs; Escape closes overlays; use `activatableProps` from `src/lib/a11y.js` for custom activators |
| Screen reader | Icon-only: `aria-label`; dialogs: `DialogTitle` + `DialogDescription` (or `aria-describedby={undefined}` intentionally); live updates via `announce()` / `role="status\|alert"` |
| Touch | Interactive targets ≥44×44px (`CONTROL.md`, Button/Input defaults). Do not use sub-44 controls for primary actions |
| Contrast | Semantic tokens (`foreground`, `muted-foreground`). No `text-*/40–50` or `foreground/45` for required reading; honor `html.high-contrast` |
| Focus | Never strip outlines without `focus-visible:ring-*` / `.focus-ring` |
| Reduced motion | `usePrefersReducedMotion` (not framer alone); CSS `html.reduce-motion`; no haptic under reduce-motion |
| Scaling | Rem-based layout; respect `theme.js` text scales (90–125%); no fixed px that break at 125% |
| High DPI | Prefer SVG / `Icon` for chrome; meaningful `alt` on content images |
| Landscape / tablet / desktop | `PageShell` clears header/nav/dock; `md:` sidebar vs bottom nav; don’t crush content on short landscape heights |

## Skip link

App chrome: skip to `#main-content`. Public pages: same pattern to main landmark.

## Definition of done

Incomplete if a primary control is &lt;44px, keyboard-unreachable, unlabeled to SR, animates under reduce-motion, or relies on low-opacity muted text for meaning.
